--
-- Receive a 1519 byte frame, that is a frame that is
-- one byte over the maximum length. It will be dropped
-- and the buffer will be recovered.
--
-- Then receive a max length frame and show that it is
-- properly received.
--
-- Then enable 1536 byte frame reception
--
-- Receive a 1537 byte frame, that is a frame that is
-- one byte over the maximum length. It will be dropped
-- and the buffer will be recovered.
--
-- Then receive a 1536 length frame and show that it is
-- properly received.
--
-- Check the statistics registers and observe that the
-- excessive length frame has been recorded.
--

